# Issue #376: accepted trivy findings, same ignore-list-with-justification
# shape as docker/cis-hardening.ignore and android/.mobsf. Used by both the
# `trivy config` (misconfig) and `trivy fs --scanners secret` steps in
# .github/workflows/container-hardening.yml.
#
# Add an entry only for a finding that's been reviewed and deliberately
# accepted, one ID per line, with a comment above it naming the finding and
# why it's safe.

# DS-0002 (HIGH) — "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile": no
# Dockerfile in this repo has a USER instruction, by design. The container
# runs as root at PID 1 so docker/entrypoint.sh can remap PUID/PGID
# (usermod/groupmod need root), then supervisord drops the backend to
# appuser (docker/supervisord.conf:20). Mirrors the 4.1 WARN acceptance in
# docker/cis-hardening.ignore; an explicit `USER root` would still fail the
# CIS check. This was triaged from the first real run before hard-gating
# the misconfig step (issue #578).
DS-0002
